  "reason": "The current best config (config_019: PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) achieves 0.639 acc. Key evidence shows multiprofile and weighted fusion are strong, avgpool beats transformer, and image encoder choice (ResNet50 vs ViT-L) makes negligible difference. The major untested axis is the RNA encoder: all experiments so far use PCA (a simple linear projection). config_031 (scvi_n200, ResNet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) is a clean single-variable change from config_019, isolating whether a learned nonlinear RNA representation (scVI latent) can outperform PCA. This is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve: if scvi_n200 improves performance, it opens a productive exploration direction for RNA encoders; if not, it confirms PCA is sufficient and we can focus budget on other axes. Under a limited budget, this experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about an important design choice while maintaining all other settings at their empirically validated best values."
}

